et_id":"5e30-f7f7-ece9-4ceb"},{"link_uuid":"fd4e2b15-af72-49e5-a8f9-d84d059694ff","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f947-77c7-851e-45a8"},{"link_uuid":"a785d54c-31c4-41ed-a3d4-49f2fe1e58ca","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e076-a2d7-ec80-4ee9"},{"link_uuid":"b301eb53-1de9-448c-8a32-3289574a67b2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"9aa3-e9f9-24c3-4427"},{"link_uuid":"751bd05c-e6a5-44e5-91c6-8182cd371386","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"251b-9e71-2ba1-4127"},{"link_uuid":"821c186d-20c6-4d12-8f2e-8c1a4ce839ba","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b996-e471-c055-48ee"},{"link_uuid":"3374e6f1-e695-4b35-ab7c-2d4f0c6935e7","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b343-139b-ba81-4636"},{"link_uuid":"a015276a-14f7-4d85-ab79-4d66ef3a91a4","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3441-c0d7-449b-48b3"},{"link_uuid":"492564b4-4ae9-4bd4-8a56-32f30a50b06f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b1a2-f5ac-d907-46f5"},{"link_uuid":"915b54f0-aae3-4593-8d2e-0caa0510214d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"975e-5e5c-cadf-4c18"},{"link_uuid":"a08617ef-78a0-47d7-9578-251390528ca5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"4f46-3942-36ee-42c6"},{"link_uuid":"06b3e7f1-1ac1-47c8-ae19-f11a793000dd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"93f4-b524-ef9b-46d9"},{"link_uuid":"24cd6774-00d9-4fe9-bd73-676b6591f1ba","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1132-be96-eea7-48ea"},{"link_uuid":"8f85777b-7c04-404f-a28f-7ece0543ea50","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6731-2e42-be10-441a"},{"link_uuid":"539327b2-d167-4d7e-b58d-cf3f3f0ccbe9","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c675-b07b-d5de-4038"},{"link_uuid":"ccccc784-841a-467d-925e-473582ea8d65","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b9f5-b4d2-3715-4ce1"},{"link_uuid":"7912a34d-ae2a-484b-ac26-4b82826732e6","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d544-29b3-8317-454f"},{"link_uuid":"eedb0a04-b025-4371-aac4-5feca37b0a51","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"083c-657a-e81f-4882"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_canonical_consolidation.py:1-18` — Preserve pre-change golden independence and encoding axes. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py:1-32, 107-113, 154-160` — Preserve propagation/level fail-open mechanisms and both logger roots. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_cas_backoff_refetch_baldish.py:1-11` — Preserve sleep→fetch ordering and jitter behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_caused_by_dedup_10d0.py:1-18` — Preserve idempotent explicit attribution, replacement, and blame fallback. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_caused_by_provenance.py:1-19` — Preserve explicit/derived/legacy event shapes. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_change_input_not_an_outage_43d4.py:1-16, 164-171, 211-218, 246-253, 308-316` — Preserve typed classification, exception-order mechanism, overreach controls, and close-screen propagation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_changed_criteria.py:1-13, 225-229` — Preserve offline selection/error contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_check_build_env_locked.py:1-15, 99-105` — Preserve parsed lock/freeze comparison, allowlist, and PEP 503 normalization. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py:195-200, 294-298` — Preserve Git-scoped file selection and fixture gate stubbing. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py:1-18` — Preserve derived-set, mutation-teeth, exclusions, and local-gate wiring. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py:1-15` — Preserve cross-language interpolation hazard and declared-variable awareness. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_child_env_concurrency.py:1-17` — Preserve concurrent overlay isolation and unchanged `os.environ`. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_child_env.py:1-19` — Preserve ownership projection and non-mutation contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_child_oracle_fail_open.py:1-50, 96-101, 108-113, 239-256, 278-284` — Preserve negative-returncode boundary, empty-output hazard, real-site testing reason, and deterministic self-kill setup. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_actionlint_install.py:1-13, 25-29, 79-82` — Preserve fail-fast install, nested-import bootstrap, and signal-kill oracle guard. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_actionlint_scope.py:1-12` — Preserve all-workflow actionlint scope and distinction from parity checks. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py:1-30, 185-193` — Preserve no-main-push policy, preserved topic pushes, schedules, dispatch, and CodeQL cadence. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py:1-37, 161-167, 352-359, 459-464, 501-506, 540-545, 563-566` — Preserve provider isolation, overlay shape/layering, credentials, region, readiness, and provider-family mapping. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env 